    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "b81jlg",
      "x": -420,
      "y": 47700,
      "name": "Row — Admin — Views",
      "width": 300,
      "height": 760,
      "content": "Admin — Views\n\nPlatform-counted content views (table ContentView). Seven subject types are recorded: Devlogs, Blog posts, Courses, Events, Experts, Vacancies, Projects. The seven are disjoint — ProjectPage counts /project/[projectSlug] only, devlogs are ProjectReport on /devlog/[projectReportId] — so the series are additive. Scout pages have no public page yet and are left out entirely.\n\nFour blocks: header + range control, seven KPI cards in one row, one multi-line chart by day, Top 10 per type behind a seven-way segmented control. Every Top 10 title is a link to the item's public page — ink at rest, link colour plus an underline on hover, graphite focus ring.\n\nRange presets (7 / 30 / 90) live inside the RangePicker, the way the audit log does it — no second control repeating them. Hard bound: 90 days, because a retention cron prunes raw rows and a longer range would silently read as zero. The picker disables earlier dates and says why in its footer.\n\nDENSITY matches the admin tab: 56px rows, 44px table head, first column indented to 24.\n\nDEBT — the panels are deliberately filled (--gd-color-surface + hairline --gd-color-border, radius 12) rather than outlined as the guidelines require. Users, Roles and the audit log all carry a filled card, and one transparent page in the same tab reads as unfinished. The fill lives in ModernTable's .modernTableWrapper, which 18 screens share, so flipping it belongs to its own task. No literals here: when that role changes, this page follows for free. Radius is 12, not the neighbours' 8 — 8 is not on the ladder.\n\nThe series palette is validated at the 3:1 mark threshold, not the 4.5:1 text one: colour lives on the 2px line, the hover dot and an 8x8 square, while every label is set in --gd-color-text. It also sits at exactly the 8.0 CVD target, so end labels, the all-series tooltip and legend isolation are the identity channel, not decoration.\n\nToken names and hex values live in docs/design/specs/admin-views.md, not on the canvas.\n\nTo the right: loading, empty, error, the isolated-series chart, the Top 10 link states, and the range picker with the bound visible."
    },
