              "content": "The title carries the link, not the row. At rest it stays ink: ten orange lines per screen, times seven types, would turn the table into a palisade and drain the accent of meaning. The affordance arrives on hover — --gd-color-link plus an underline, because colour alone is not an affordance and a hover a colour-blind reader cannot see is not a hover — and on focus as a graphite ring in --gd-color-border-focus at focusRingWidth 3. Truncation to one line with a tooltip is unchanged. Row metrics match the admin tab: 56px rows, 44px head, first column indented to 24.",
