    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "DVlqv",
      "x": 9500,
      "y": 10555,
      "name": "Note — Hub — Welcome character",
      "width": 300,
      "height": 340,
      "content": "Hub — Welcome character\n\nPage chrome matches the app: header $surface with a bottom border, page background $page-bg, content gutter 50 / top 36 / bottom 16, grid 1fr + 320 with gap 24. Every hub section is TRANSPARENT — only a 1px $card-border and radius 16; the page background shows through (hubSection.module.scss: background: transparent). Welcome and feed are two separate cards stacked with gap 24, not one bundle.\n\nWelcomeHero: padding 24, title 22/700/1.25, subtitle 15/1.5 capped at 520. Height is content-driven (~103).\n\nCharacter: replaces the abstract lines. Assets welcome-character-female.png / welcome-character-male.png (transparent PNG). A 144-wide wrapper inset 24 from the card's right edge starts 32px above the top border and ends at the bottom border — it is the only node that clips, so the head overflows the top border while the body is cut by the bottom one. The card must not clip it, so the wrapper is a sibling of the card, not a child.\nFemale art: 144x156 at 0,0. Male art: 132x143 at 6,5 (his head reads bigger, so he is scaled down to match).\n\nSelection: one of the two is picked at random once per session, on sign-in, and stays stable for the whole session. Sign out and back in re-rolls it.\n\nNot updated yet: Hub Page — Mobile (/hub) still shows the old artwork.\n\nThe 32px overhang is what keeps the crossed arms above the bottom border. With a 103-tall card, character size and arm visibility trade off against that overhang, and the 36px of page padding above the card is its ceiling."
    },
